<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Which graph correctly shows the solution to the inequality <span>\( \dfrac{7x-3}9 \geq 8-2x \)</span>? Show or explain your reasoning.</para>
    <div>
      <para>A</para><media><image alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2e5181154134c7cd7fc2b5f7dae48b8a06531e2a"/>
    </media></div>
    <div>
      <para>B</para><media><image alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3ea0124440695580d09e2ee8f6912aa1bc04e133"/>
    </media></div>
    <div>
      <para>C</para><media><image alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.&#10;" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5f9cbe1e285f06fba5115a39c71b867bf673514b"/>
    </media></div>
    <div>
      <para>D</para><media><image alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/804e2763d72ce690ee98333f42fa3d04c68773e4"/></media></div>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answers may vary, but here are some samples. Graph C.</para>
    <list>
      <item>I tested 2, 3, and 4 for the values of \(x\), and 3 and 4 make the inequality true.</item>
      <item>I solved a related equation and then tested a couple of values on either side of the solution.</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
